{"id":"4047365","slug":"josh-jacobs","name":"Josh Jacobs","position":"RB","team":"GB","headshot":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/nfl/players/full/4047365.png","formats":{"ppr-12":{"positionRank":67,"ourRank":262,"vorRound":22,"adp":92.6,"projected":30.80879904021756,"vor":-58.09648541104164,"expectedGames":3.4762260481002834,"floor":null,"median":null,"ceiling":null,"tier":13,"preseasonRank":125,"preseasonPoints":110.72},"half-ppr-12":{"positionRank":66,"ourRank":267,"vorRound":23,"adp":84.8,"projected":27.52357783368881,"vor":-48.23602685920054,"expectedGames":3.4762260481002834,"floor":null,"median":null,"ceiling":null,"tier":11,"preseasonRank":123,"preseasonPoints":104.35},"standard-12":{"positionRank":65,"ourRank":286,"vorRound":24,"adp":77.7,"projected":24.241073931714666,"vor":-37.53466579114196,"expectedGames":3.4762260481002834,"floor":null,"median":null,"ceiling":null,"tier":12,"preseasonRank":134,"preseasonPoints":83.96}},"capsule":{"body":"Drafters have moved off him fast, sliding 29 picks in three weeks, and they still have not gone far enough. We have him at 111 points, RB38 on our board, while his ADP sits at 93. That gap is not a rounding error, it is a full round of somebody else's bench.\n\nThe reason is scoring, not workload. His 35.4% touchdown-points share costs him 9.6 points a game against expectation, and the 20.9% red-zone touch share another 6.4. Last season he scored above the weekly median in 12 of 15 games and finished RB13, so the talent is real. But he turns 29 this year, and our projection expects 13 games with a range that dips to 6. The injury designation from mid-October does not help.\n\nThen there is the head-scratcher on the roster sheet: he is listed fourth among GB running backs, behind Chris Brooks and Kaleb Johnson. That may be camp bookkeeping, but combined with the touchdown flags it reads like a team preparing for less Jacobs. His snap share fell from 74% in weeks 1 to 4 down to 48% by weeks 14 to 17 last year, so the slide was already happening before the depth chart move. Inside-ten touches were RB6 last year, which is what keeps him startable when he plays, and the 82-to-139 middle range still covers a usable RB2 stretch. Matt LaFleur calls the plays himself and is back, so nobody is coming in to redraw the offense around him.\n\nOur call: let him go at pick 93. If he slides four or five picks past that, take him as your third back and accept the volatility. Any earlier is a reach on a name that scored RB6 two years ago, not this one.","pulls":[{"figure":"111","caption":"projected PPR points"},{"figure":"93","caption":"his ADP in PPR drafts"}]},"season":{"season":2026,"format":"ppr-12","weeks":18,"through":5,"games":0,"pointsPerGame":null,"totals":{"pass_attempts":null,"completions":null,"passing_yards":null,"passing_touchdowns":null,"interceptions":null,"carries":null,"rushing_yards":null,"rushing_touchdowns":null,"targets":null,"receptions":null,"receiving_yards":null,"receiving_touchdowns":null,"fumbles_lost":null,"field_goals_made":null,"extra_points_made":null,"sacks":null,"defensive_interceptions":null,"defensive_touchdowns":null,"snapShare":null,"points":null},"log":[{"pass_attempts":null,"completions":null,"passing_yards":null,"passing_touchdowns":null,"interceptions":null,"carries":null,"rushing_yards":null,"rushing_touchdowns":null,"targets":null,"receptions":null,"receiving_yards":null,"receiving_touchdowns":null,"fumbles_lost":null,"field_goals_made":null,"extra_points_made":null,"sacks":null,"defensive_interceptions":null,"defensive_touchdowns":null,"snapShare":null,"points":null,"week":1,"opponent":"MIN","home":false,"status":"inactive"},{"pass_attempts":null,"completions":null,"passing_yards":null,"passing_touchdowns":null,"interceptions":null,"carries":null,"rushing_yards":null,"rushing_touchdowns":null,"targets":null,"receptions":null,"receiving_yards":null,"receiving_touchdowns":null,"fumbles_lost":null,"field_goals_made":null,"extra_points_made":null,"sacks":